   254	- **Phase 2 (v1.6.0):** Health scoring composer migrated to consume `scoring::factors`; `compute_account_health` made pure; DB-history writes extracted to a maintenance ability per [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md).
   255	
   256	### R1.2 Health scoring determinism requires extracting writes first
   257	
   258	Codex flagged: `compute_account_health` is not pure today — it mutates DB history inside the compute call. The ADR's claim of "deterministic scoring under fixture replay" is false until writes are split out.
   259	
   260	**Revised:** Phase 2 explicitly extracts the history-write side effect. The refactor:
   261	
   262	```rust
   263	// Before
   264	fn compute_account_health(entity_id: &str, db: &Db) -> HealthScore { /* computes + writes history */ }
   265	
   266	// After
   267	fn compute_account_health_pure(inputs: HealthScoringInputs, clock: &Clock) -> HealthScore { /* pure */ }
