     1	//! Signal event CRUD and source tier weights (ADR-0080).
     2	//!
     3	//! ## Signal Taxonomy (I530)
     4	//!
     5	//! User-facing actions emit these signal types:
     6	//!
     7	//! | Signal Type              | Source           | Weight Change       | Trigger                |
     8	//! |--------------------------|------------------|---------------------|------------------------|
     9	//! | `intelligence_confirmed` | `user_feedback`  | alpha += 1          | Thumbs up (I529)       |
    10	//! | `intelligence_rejected`  | `user_feedback`  | beta  += 1          | Thumbs down (I529)     |
    11	//! | `user_correction`        | `user_edit`      | beta  += 1          | Edit intelligence field |
    12	//! | `intelligence_curated`   | `user_curation`  | (no weight change)  | Delete / remove item   |
    13	//! | `email_signal_dismissed` | `user_correction`| (no weight change)  | Dismiss email signal   |
    14	//! | `email_item_dismissed`   | (item_type)      | (no weight change)  | Dismiss email item     |
    15	//!
    16	//! Corrections (edit, thumbs-down) penalize the wrong source. Curation (delete,
    17	//! dismiss) records user preference without penalizing—the AI wasn't necessarily
    18	//! wrong, the user just doesn't need that item.
    19	
