.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2263:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:504:.docs/decisions/0126-memory-substrate-invariants.md:48:Explicit user judgment (correction, tombstone, confirmation) flows through `claim_feedback` per ADR-0123 typed feedback semantics. Explicit judgment affects trust via DOS-5's `fb` factor.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2264:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:508:.docs/decisions/0126-memory-substrate-invariants.md:90:- Feedback events (correction, confirmation, tombstone) → `claim_feedback` (ADR-0123 typed) → DOS-5's `fb` factor → trust.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2265:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:512:.docs/decisions/0126-memory-substrate-invariants.md:121:- **`user_dismissed_soft` as a surfacing demotion reason.** User intent is a tombstone (`claim_state='tombstoned'`), not a system surfacing decision.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2269:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:669:.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:11:[ADR-0114](0114-scoring-unification.md) R1.7 placed `user_feedback_weight` as a canonical scoring factor and referenced a `FeedbackAction` enum with placeholder values `StillTrue | Outdated | WrongSource`. [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) §6 declared the agent trust-ledger updates as "User accepts an agent claim → α += 1 / User contradicts → β += 1" without typing accept vs. contradict.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2271:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:676:.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:140:- `scoring::factors::user_feedback_weight(feedback: Option<&UserFeedbackInput>)` (ADR-0114 R1.3) consumes a `UserFeedbackInput { action: FeedbackAction, age_days: f64 }`. Pure; the extractor pulls latest feedback per claim per ADR-0114 §2.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2302:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:972:.docs/decisions/0118-dailyos-as-ai-harness-principles-and-residual-gaps.md:111:**Where this lands.** [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) §5 now specifies tombstones concretely: `actor = 'user'` or `user_removal`, `claim_text = NULL`, `retraction_reason = 'user_removal'`, `claim_state = 'committed'`. §3's commit policy gate includes a hard check against recent tombstones at the target `field_path` — an agent claim targeting a tombstoned field within the tombstone window (default 30 days) is rejected before it enters `proposed` state. Gap D is subsumed.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2317:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1503:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:8:**Consumed by:** [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) (`intelligence_claims.actor` column, tombstones), [DOS-241](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-241) (enrichment refactor design)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2326:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1527:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:295:**Consolidation timing — 2026-04-20 update:** Per plan-eng-review AskUserQuestion #1 and the brownfield-as-greenfield founder commitment (D1), consolidation ships in v1.4.0 as a destructive migration alongside the `intelligence_claims` table creation. Original R1.3 deferred consolidation to v1.4.1 out of migration caution; that deferral is retracted. Rationale: at AI velocity + minimal user base, keeping three parallel tombstone mechanisms alive through v1.4.0 creates interop cost that exceeds consolidation cost. The interop is what's expensive; one-table-to-rule-them-all is cleaner.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2327:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1528:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:302:- Reads switch to `intelligence_claims` for all tombstone queries.
