.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:2894:.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:157:**Trust-score micro-drift suppression.** `ClaimTrustChanged` fires only on **band-boundary crossings** (`likely_current` ↔ `use_with_caution` ↔ `needs_verification`). A trust score drifting from 0.72 to 0.73 does not emit; 0.71 to 0.69 (crossing the `likely_current → use_with_caution` boundary) does. The band is computed in the Trust Compiler ([DOS-5](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-5)) and passed into the emit check.
